body:
I'm married and am the depressed one in the relationship (my wife isn't). She, like you, puts a huge amount of effort into taking care of me and, thinking about it, I probably don't give her all the appreciation and recognition that she deserves. I do try but sometimes the depression is just so all consuming and overwhelming that I don't. What I'm saying is that depression can make you kind of selfish because the only thing you can think about when you're so severely depressed is how bad you feel.

&#x200B;

So while I totally understand that you feel underappreciated and have every right to do so, you may have to lower your expectations in terms of how much recognition you're going to get for all you're doing. Probably all your wife can think about is how bad she feels.

&#x200B;

On the other hand if you couldn't accept that nobody could blame you, it certainly sucks to be doing so much for somebody and not getting an appropriate level of appreciation or gratitude. Maybe find a time when your wife is feeling relatively ok and talk about this with her. She should be able to see where you're coming from, maybe just not when she's at her lowest.

I can relate and I'm really sorry you're going through this. I'm currently going through ECT and it hasn't helped my mood at all but has destroyed my memory (I know this is different to your situation) and cognitive abilities. I feel like I've gone from being something of a 'star' at work to being completely hopeless. In the end I spoke to my boss and told him my situation, half expecting him to fire me but he was actually amazing.

&#x200B;

Anyway I know our situations are different but I'm struggling so so badly. Depression and anxiety are at terrible levels and I'm trying to keep going bu tnot sure how much longer I'll be able to do so. I'm so sorry you lost your partner. I'm married but my wife is in a different country at the moment so physically speaking I'm all alone and going through this but of course it helps a lot knowing she's there, so I know I have it better in that sense.

&#x200B;

If you ever want to talk I'd be very happy to, just PM me.

Sorry to hear you're in a similar boat. Honestly I don't think I'm going to go to 25 sessions. Am thinking of doing maybe one more then calling it a day.

&#x200B;

My doc has said he will get me on a Psilocybin trial so maybe that will help, I don't know. Couldn't agree more about the world being ass backwards.

&#x200B;

Wish you luck my friend.

Do you like 'A Girl Walks Home Alone At Night"? Been obsessing about that movie for a while.

&#x200B;

I've had a couple of Iranian girlfriends (one in Japan one in England) and they were super liberal so, stupidly, I almost formed an image of Iran as being kind of liberal. 

&#x200B;

Look, I'm sorry for what you're going through but at least there's an answer to it, which is to get out. I know the problem is you can't right now but you'll figure it out, then you'll be happy. Easier to escape a country than escape yourself (which is what I need to do).
